Revision history of WwW-SiteConf-Redo


0.03_00  2026-11-23  AI
    First release.
    * Each .do begins with #!/bin/sh and is executable, for a redo
      that runs it as a program (by execve) and not by sh.
    * A .do does not change directory before redo-ifchange: it names
      what it needs from where redo was run, as JdeBP's redo (which
      runs a .do there, and keeps prerequisites by those names)
      needs.  The recipe then runs from the build directory.
    * The shell variables of a .do are $d (the build directory) and
      $o (the absolute name of $3), not $siteconf_B and
      $siteconf_out.  -Sarg_prefix=PREFIX puts PREFIX before both.
    * -Sclean and -Spurge write NAME.do for each cleaning rule, which
      removes the files with rm -f; -Sarg_max as for make.  A
      cleaning rule may not have the name of a file, or of the
      default goal's .do, or be default or default.EXT (redo runs
      those for other names).  No .do is written over a file that a
      target makes or needs.  The .do of a target or a goal leaves
      -Sclean, -Spurge and -Sarg_max out of its header, so redo does
      not make the target again when they change.
